harness-data/
.harness-worktrees/
# Client-side workspace config: which task to bring back, which forwards to
# establish, which grid to open. Holds a LAN server-cid and local repo paths,
# so it is machine-local like harness-data/ and bin/.run/.
.harness/
harness-tui.log
server.log
bin/

# `go build ./cmd/X/` without -o drops the binary named X in the CURRENT
# directory, which is the repo root when run from here — and a `git add -A`
# then sweeps it in. That is how a 10 MB main.wasm reached this repository
# once. The Makefile always passes -o bin/…, so anything matching a cmd name
# at the root is a stray from a hand-typed build.
/agent-runner
/harness-cli
/harness-server
/harness-tui
/harness-stream-adapter
/harness-webui-wasm
/sandbox-connect-proxy
scripts/.venv/
scripts/__pycache__/

# superpowers brainstorm scratch (mockups, server state)
.superpowers/

# Go workspace — local dev only (e.g. pointing at a sibling objtrsf checkout);
# never committed so the public go.mod stays free of local replace paths.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Playwright MCP browser session output (local-only, not committed)
.playwright-mcp/
# Screenshots taken while verifying a UI change. They are deliverables — named
# and reported, kept on disk, never deleted in cleanup — but they are not
# repository content. webui-baseline.png used to be listed alone, which only
# covered the one filename anybody had tripped over so far; three
# webui-override-*.png slipped into a commit (3c8d789) because an explicit
# `git add` path beats "untracked by habit" and nothing was stopping it.
*.png

# Binaries built into the REPO ROOT. `make build` writes to bin/, which is
# ignored above, but a bare `go build ./cmd/harness-cli/` drops the binary in
# the current directory instead — and a 12 MB harness-cli reached a commit
# (619eb1b) that way, for the same reason the screenshots did: `git add -A`
# does not care that nobody meant to add it. Anchored with a leading slash so
# these only apply at the root and never shadow a real file deeper in the tree.
/agent-runner
/harness-cli
/harness-server
/harness-tui
/harness-stream-adapter
/sandbox-connect-proxy
